#. ~ Description of NPC faction "PrepNet Phyle"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid ""
"A multitude of frontier homesteading groups brought together by their use of "
"the PrepNet communication protocols.  Spread out onto the edges of the "
"frontier, enthusiastically squatting and building tiny kingdoms often "
"consisting of just a couple families or like-minded individuals.  Their "
"mutual aid societies are wildly varied in their laws; influenced by the "
"people who set them up, but they all share in a distrust for those that wish "
"to impose restrictions upon new colonization efforts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC faction name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid "United Interstellar Coordination Agency"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of NPC faction "United Interstellar Coordination Agency"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid ""
"A loose confederation and military alliance composed by Solar Corporations, Governments, and other politically relevant organizations united by their desire to restore Earth's dominion over the Orion Arm.  Due to the disinterest of the Salus Charter owners and the recent rediscovery of the system, UICA administers Salus IV using a combination of military and civilian law designed to maximize wealth extraction, with the bulk of their forces concentrated within Port Augustmoon.\n"
"\n"
"Corruption and nepotism are rampant across UICA's frontier administrations, management is generally more interested in lining their own pockets than in any sort of solar revanchist rhetoric."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC faction name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid "Wraitheon Industries ltd."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of NPC faction "Wraitheon Industries ltd."
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid ""
"A massive, multi-system corporation with major investments across artificial "
"intelligence, shipbuilding, military cybernetics and applied robotics.  Among"
" the oldest of the Solar Corporations, it is a major player in the Orion Arm,"
" and a key military supplier of UICA's military hardware.  It is best known "
"for its normally secretive and highly advanced research and archaeology "
"division."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC faction name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid "Mercurial Genomics ltd."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of NPC faction "Mercurial Genomics ltd."
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid ""
"A massive, multi-system corporation specializing in genetic engineering, "
"terraforming, and biotechnology.  Before the discontinuity, it heavily "
"invested in extrasolar colonization and the study of alien life.  "
"Theoretically it holds the planetary colonization charter for Salus IV, per "
"UICA's constitional treaty, but the corporation's interests currently lie "
"elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC faction name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid "Independents"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of NPC faction "Independents"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/factions.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/factions.json
msgid ""
"A loose group of salvors, mercenaries and frontiersmen working as free agents"
" or in representation of interest groups too small or remote to have official"
" presence in the system.  Equally likely to cooperate among themselves as "
"they are to fight each other."
msgstr ""

